<title>SPAIN: Spain had 64.4 bln pta May current a/c surplus.</title>
<headline>Spain had 64.4 bln pta May current a/c surplus.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain gave the following figures (in billions of pesetas):</p>
<p> BALANCE OF PAYMENTS		MAY 97    APR 97     MAY 96</p>
<p>  C/A balance			 64.4	 14.2	-22.3</p>
<p>  Trade balance		   -143.5     -208.3     -210.2</p>
<p>  Services			   243.1	229.3	212.9</p>
<p>  Net tourism receipts	   272.1	259.0	238.2</p>
<p>  Other services		   -29.0	-29.7	-25.3</p>
<p>  Dividend income		  -45.6	-46.3	-48.3</p>
<p>  Transfers			   10.5	 39.6	 23.4</p>
<p>  CAPITAL ACCOUNT		   27.2	 76.8	 39.5</p>
<p>  FINANCIAL ACCOUNT		 -5.0	-94.5	 -0.9</p>
<p>  Spanish investment abroad   -178.8     -178.2	  1.6</p>
<p>  Foreign investment in Spain  883.1	459.3     -103.3</p>
<p>  Spanish loans,deposits abroa-646.2	563.5	145.0</p>
<p>  Foreign loans, deps in Spain  12.9     -797.3	364.3</p>
<p>  Movement of reserves	   -75.9     -141.8     -408.6</p>
<p>NOTE: The Bank of Spain said latest figures were provisional. Non-classified element (errors and omissions) in latest capital account figures is negative 86.7 billion pesetas. The financial account category was introduced in January 1996.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
